    "evidence_text": "Treatment of nonalcoholic fatty liver disease: role of AMPK.\n\nIn addition, we examine the mechanisms by which AMPK is activated.\n\nAMPK also suppresses inflammation.\n\nLy6Chi monocytes direct alternatively activated profibrotic macrophage regulation of lung fibrosis.\n\nRATIONALE Idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF) is a devastating disease.\n\nAntiinflammatory therapies, including corticosteroids, are of no benefit.\n\nThe role of monocytes and macrophages is therefore controversial.   \n\n\nFurther studies were performed on samples from patients with IPF.   \n\n\nActivation of AMP-activated protein kinase suppresses oxidized low-density lipoprotein-induced macrophage proliferation.\n\nThese effects of AMPK activation may represent therapeutic targets for atherosclerosis.\n\nWe show that these early pathophysiological changes are accompanied by a paradoxical decrease in AMPK activity.\n\nActivation of AMPK\u03b12 in adipocytes is essential for nicotine-induced insulin resistance in vivo\n\nHowever, the mechanisms behind these effects are unclear.\n\nMetformin reverses established lung fibrosis in a bleomycin model\n\nCellular metabolism regulates tissue repair and remodelling responses to injury2-4.\n\nHowever, the role of AMPK in fibrosis is not well understood.",
